# WEEK 9 – Create and Push Docker Image to AWS ECR

## 1. Navigate to the project directory

```bash
cd ~/week9
```

## 2. Display the Dockerfile

```bash
cat Dockerfile
```

## 3. Build the Docker image

```bash
sudo docker build -t week9-repo .
```

## 4. List Docker images

```bash
sudo docker images
```

## 5. Run the Docker image and show output

```bash
sudo docker run --rm week9-repo:latest
```

Expected output:

```text
Week 9 - Docker image pushed to AWS ECR successfully!
```

## 6. Tag the image for AWS ECR

```bash
sudo docker tag week9-repo:latest 879343933306.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/week9-repo:latest
```

## 7. Authenticate with AWS ECR

```bash
aws ecr get-login-password --region ap-south-1 | sudo docker login --username AWS --password-stdin 879343933306.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com
```

Expected output: `Login Succeeded`

## 8. Push the image to AWS ECR

```bash
sudo docker push 879343933306.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/week9-repo:latest
```

Expected result: image layers are pushed and a digest is displayed.

## 9. Verify the image

Open AWS Console → Amazon ECR → Private registry → Repositories → `week9-repo`.

Verify that the image tag `latest` is present and its status is Active.

## Result

Successfully created a Docker image and pushed it to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (ECR).
